### Lab 7: Microsoft Search API checks for the hleTickets connection.
### Run in Graph Explorer (https://developer.microsoft.com/graph/graph-explorer) signed in AS THE PERSONA you are testing.
### Delegated permission: see the "Permissions" table of POST /search/query on Learn (ExternalItem.Read.All is expected; confirm).
### Results are security trimmed by each item's ACL, so the same request returns different results per persona.

### 1. Find ticket 104321 (deny beats grant): Marcus and the learner get no hit, Priya and Sofia get one.
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/search/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "entityTypes": ["externalItem"],
      "contentSources": ["/external/connections/hleTickets"],
      "query": { "queryString": "ticketId:104321" },
      "fields": ["ticketId", "title", "status", "url", "lastModified"],
      "from": 0,
      "size": 5
    }
  ]
}

### 2. Free text: HR case HR-2026-0381 (only HR group members get ticket 102050).
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/search/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "entityTypes": ["externalItem"],
      "contentSources": ["/external/connections/hleTickets"],
      "query": { "queryString": "HR-2026-0381" },
      "fields": ["ticketId", "title", "status", "url"],
      "size": 5
    }
  ]
}

### 3. Refiner check: count of visible tickets by region (region is refinable, schema-design.md 2).
### The Learn aggregation example uses the beta endpoint. If v1.0 rejects "aggregations", run this one on beta.
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/search/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "entityTypes": ["externalItem"],
      "contentSources": ["/external/connections/hleTickets"],
      "query": { "queryString": "*" },
      "aggregations": [ { "field": "region", "size": 5, "bucketDefinition": { "sortBy": "count", "isDescending": true, "minimumCount": 0 } } ],
      "size": 1
    }
  ]
}

### 4. Indexing check (C-07-c): run right after ingestion and again later; record the time and totals.
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/search/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "entityTypes": ["externalItem"],
      "contentSources": ["/external/connections/hleTickets"],
      "query": { "queryString": "Toronto Head Office parking P2" },
      "fields": ["ticketId", "title", "url"],
      "size": 5
    }
  ]
}
